    "statement": "Demography alone raises age-related outlays from 10 % of GDP in 2024 to a median 24.1 % by 2100 in depopulating economies, and that pressure is the same under either elasticity. What the elasticity decides is what the transfer buys: the sustainable real benefit per retiree in 2100 is a median 9.0 % lower under eps=0.98/1.22 than under eps=0.92, per-capita output doubles a median 3 years later, and holding the debt ratio constant costs a further 0.12 pp of GDP a year for every 100 % of GDP of initial debt."
